Less waiting for the GPU on the game thread. A pixel metric (Delfino's
pollution counts) is answered from the newest of the last two frames' queries
that has come back, not always the last frame's, which the GPU has often not
finished yet; an EFB copy's write-back to RAM is stored once the GL thread
has read it, or a frame later. Waiting for the previous frame's results kept
the game from starting a frame while the GPU caught up (about 4 ms a frame in
Delfino Plaza on the Switch).

